From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pi-hrx-fabric <fabric@1bit.local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:2x:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] accel/amdxdna: don't re-invalidate imported dma-buf BOs
 from the mmu notifier

amdxdna_hmm_invalidate() applies the same marking that amdxdna_insert_pages() used to apply at mmap
time. For an imported BO that is just as wrong: any real invalidation of the range - typically the
exporter calling unmap_mapping_range() while it evicts or migrates the buffer - would put the BO back on
client->bo_invalid_list, and the next submit would return -EFAULT for the entire client again.

Skip the invalidation marking for imported BOs, but keep the sequence update and the MMU_NOTIFY_UNMAP
cleanup for them: readers waiting in mmu_interval_read_retry() must still make progress, and the
notifier must still be unregistered when the range is unmapped.

Same provenance and the same status as the previous patch: rebased onto this directory's series, NOT
installed, owner-gated (#812), compile-proven (srcversion 336751493A77C50DE0B50F7).

Signed-off-by: bong-water-water-bong <bong-water-water-bong@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_drm.c |  6 +++---
 drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_gem.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_gem.c
@@ -317,10 +317,19 @@
 		 client && amdxdna_client_has_pending_jobs(client));
 
 	down_write(&xdna->notifier_lock);
-	if (client && !abo->dying && list_empty(&abo->node))
-		list_add_tail(&abo->node, &client->bo_invalid_list);
-	abo->mem.map_invalid = true;
-	mapp->invalid = true;
+	/*
+	 * An imported BO's population and migration belong to its exporter: any real invalidation of that range
+	 * (typically the exporter calling unmap_mapping_range() while it evicts or migrates) would put the BO back on
+	 * client->bo_invalid_list, and the next submit of the process would fail -EFAULT for every job, not just for
+	 * the one touching the range. The sequence update and the unmap cleanup below stay: readers waiting in
+	 * mmu_interval_read_retry() must make progress, and the notifier must be unregistered on unmap.
+	 */
+	if (!is_import_bo(abo)) {
+		if (client && !abo->dying && list_empty(&abo->node))
+			list_add_tail(&abo->node, &client->bo_invalid_list);
+		abo->mem.map_invalid = true;
+		mapp->invalid = true;
+	}
 	mmu_interval_set_seq(&mapp->notifier, cur_seq);
 	if (range->event == MMU_NOTIFY_UNMAP && !mapp->unmapped) {
 		queue_work(xdna->notifier_wq, &mapp->hmm_unreg_work);
--- a/drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/amdxdna/amdxdna_drm.c
@@ -166,10 +166,9 @@
 	list_del(&client->node);
 	amdxdna_hwctx_remove_all(client);
 	/*
-	 * amdxdna_hmm_invalidate() and amdxdna_mark_mapp_invalid() copy
-	 * abo->client and then hold client->hwctx_srcu while they link the BO
-	 * into client->bo_invalid_list and wait for the hardware contexts to go
-	 * idle.  amdxdna_hwctx_destroy_rcu() only waits for those readers when
+	 * amdxdna_hmm_invalidate() copies abo->client and then holds
+	 * client->hwctx_srcu while it links the BO into client->bo_invalid_list
+	 * and waits for the hardware contexts to go idle.  amdxdna_hwctx_destroy_rcu() only waits for those readers when
 	 * there was a hardware context left to destroy; a client that closes
 	 * with none (the normal XRT exit order destroys them by ioctl first)
 	 * got no grace period at all, so a reader that copied the pointer
